WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.729 --> 00:00:05.380
Millions of film fans hold special places
in their hearts for Forrest, Jenny, Lieutenant

00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:08.660
Dan, and the rest of the unforgettable characters
of Forrest Gump.

00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:12.099
But what happened to the ensemble in the years
since 1994?

00:00:12.099 --> 00:00:15.079
We've taken a look back to find out what these
stars have been up to.

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:20.750
Let's start with the obvious: Tom Hanks, already
an Oscar-winning mega-star when he played

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:22.940
Forrest Gump, hasn't exactly vanished from
view.

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:28.080
Hanks executive-produced the Emmy-winning
HBO miniseries Band of Brothers, played two

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:33.160
American heroes in Captain Phillips and Sully,
voiced a neurotic cowboy in Pixar's Toy Story

00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:38.120
franchise, and also became the star of Saturday
Night Live's most memorable, baffling Halloween

00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:38.620
skit.

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:41.920
"Any questions?"

00:00:42.460 --> 00:00:46.580
The award-winning actor also remains half
of one of Hollywood's most long standing marriages

00:00:46.580 --> 00:00:50.660
with wife Rita Wilson, with the two having
been married since 1988.

00:00:50.890 --> 00:00:54.980
He's gained a reputation as one of the loveliest
people in Hollywood, and he has a hobby of

00:00:54.980 --> 00:00:56.920
collecting vintage typewriters.

00:00:57.920 --> 00:01:01.760
Robin Wright was hardly an unknown when she
scored her role in Forrest Gump.

00:01:01.769 --> 00:01:05.971
Her role on the daytime drama Santa Barbara
had already earned her tons of fans, and she

00:01:05.980 --> 00:01:08.960
also starred in cult fairytale favorite The
Princess Bride.

00:01:09.250 --> 00:01:14.100
But for whatever reason, Wright spent the
next two decades flying way under the radar.

00:01:14.110 --> 00:01:17.780
It's surprising that the role that made her
a household name is one she landed at the

00:01:17.780 --> 00:01:23.370
age of 46, the ambitious, brilliant, Claire
Underwood on Netflix's House of Cards.

00:01:23.370 --> 00:01:27.920
Offscreen, Wright has become an outspoken
advocate and spokesperson for Pour Les Femmes,

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:32.200
a sleepwear company that educates and employs
women in conflict regions around the world.

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:38.380
Most of the main folks in Forrest Gump have
gone on to have long and storied acting careers,

00:01:38.380 --> 00:01:40.540
but Michael Conner Humphreys is an exception.

00:01:40.760 --> 00:01:45.000
After what could have been a breakout performance
as young Forrest, Humphreys instead quit acting

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:47.740
entirely and took a different path, joining
the Army.

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:52.210
He served four years as an infantry soldier,
with his service including an 18-month tour

00:01:52.210 --> 00:01:53.400
of duty in Iraq.

00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:57.500
According to an interview with the Daily Mail,
he tried to keep his brief stint in Hollywood

00:01:57.500 --> 00:02:01.060
a secret, but it didn't take long for his
fellow servicemembers to figure it out and

00:02:01.060 --> 00:02:02.660
give him the nickname of "Gump."

00:02:02.970 --> 00:02:07.580
Humphreys made a belated return to acting
in the 2010s, playing a soldier in the 2011

00:02:07.580 --> 00:02:11.760
indie film Pathfinders: In the Company of
Strangers, and he also scored a role on the

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:14.110
2019 TV series Knight's End.

00:02:14.110 --> 00:02:19.170
In a 2015 interview, he was said to be living
back in his birthplace of Independence, Mississippi,

00:02:19.170 --> 00:02:22.480
where he pursued a college degree in international
relations.

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:25.200
"Run, Forrest!

00:02:25.420 --> 00:02:25.920
Run!"

00:02:26.140 --> 00:02:29.280
That's Hanna Hall's biggest contribution to
the cultural zeitgeist.

00:02:29.340 --> 00:02:34.120
At the age of nine, she became known for shouting
what became Forrest Gump's most quotable line,

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:36.090
but she's also worked regularly ever since.

00:02:36.090 --> 00:02:41.769
As a teen, she scored roles in Sofia Coppola's
The Virgin Suicides and the 2007 remake of

00:02:41.769 --> 00:02:46.670
Halloween, and in more recent years she appeared
in guest roles on Criminal Minds and Masters

00:02:46.670 --> 00:02:47.280
of Sex.

00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:51.620
Despite having grown up a lot since her Forrest
Gump performance, Hall is still occasionally

00:02:51.629 --> 00:02:56.019
recognized on the street by sharp-eyed fans
who ask her to repeat her famous catchphrase.

00:02:56.019 --> 00:03:00.420
But she's said she doesn't know how to do
that Alabama accent anymore, so if you happen

00:03:00.420 --> 00:03:02.000
to see her, just don't ask.

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:07.740
Sally Field was already a multiple Oscar winner
and A-lister when she played the tenacious

00:03:07.740 --> 00:03:09.280
matriarch of the Gump family.

00:03:09.650 --> 00:03:13.580
Her legacy as an actor was rock solid no matter
what she did after Forrest Gump.

00:03:13.600 --> 00:03:14.520
But where is she now?

00:03:14.600 --> 00:03:19.340
After spending several years as a Primetime
Emmy-award-winning guest star on ER, she joined

00:03:19.340 --> 00:03:22.880
the ABC drama Brothers and Sisters, for which
she won another Emmy.

00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:27.040
She also turned up in the role of Aunt May
in the Amazing Spider-Man movies, opposite

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:27.940
Andrew Garfield.

00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:33.000
In 2017, she earned critical acclaim for playing
the challenging role of Amanda Wingfield in

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:37.750
a Broadway revival of The Glass Menagerie,
while 2018 saw her take on a key supporting

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:39.480
role in the Netflix series Maniac.

00:03:39.840 --> 00:03:43.890
Basically, she's keeping plenty busy as she
rounds the corner on her seventh decade.

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:47.020
In Sally Field's storied career, Forrest Gump
is just a footnote.

00:03:48.180 --> 00:03:53.300
After his remarkable turn as Forrest Gump's
BFF Bubba Blue, Mykelti Williamson has stayed

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:57.280
busy in Hollywood, consistently working smaller
parts on the big and small screens.

00:03:57.280 --> 00:04:01.880
Among his more prominent appearances are a
regular role on Justified that spanned three

00:04:01.880 --> 00:04:05.520
seasons, a role in the political thriller
series 24, and more.

00:04:05.650 --> 00:04:09.440
Williamson seems to specialize in playing
police officers and military men, although

00:04:09.460 --> 00:04:14.060
he did run afoul of the law when he played
Baby-O in the cult favorite Con Air.

00:04:14.060 --> 00:04:19.220
And don't think he's given up serious award-season
fare: in 2016, he was part of the cast in

00:04:19.220 --> 00:04:22.660
the Oscar-nominated Fences, directed by Denzel
Washington.

00:04:22.940 --> 00:04:26.971
Unlike some of his co stars, Williamson has
fully embraced his legacy as a Forrest Gump

00:04:26.980 --> 00:04:27.720
cast member.

00:04:27.720 --> 00:04:32.280
On Instagram, he's even celebrated his character's
signature seafood obsession with "Shrimp Saturday",

00:04:32.290 --> 00:04:36.380
in which he posts shrimp-related selfies and
solicits pictures of shrimp from fans around

00:04:36.380 --> 00:04:36.880
the globe.

00:04:37.940 --> 00:04:42.880
Gary Sinise has had no shortage of high-profile
projects since Forrest Gump, including repeated

00:04:42.890 --> 00:04:44.460
reunions with Tom Hanks.

00:04:44.460 --> 00:04:49.860
The two appeared together in Apollo 13 in
1996 and again in The Green Mile in 1999.

00:04:50.240 --> 00:04:54.770
On the small screen, Sinise has found a comfortable
home in primetime procedural drama, playing

00:04:54.770 --> 00:05:00.310
Detective Mac Taylor in the CSI franchise
from 2004 through 2013, then taking over in

00:05:00.310 --> 00:05:03.450
a lead role in the Criminal Minds franchise
in 2016.

00:05:03.450 --> 00:05:08.230
In a fitting turn, considering his military
"experience" in Forrest Gump, Sinise has become

00:05:08.230 --> 00:05:11.120
a prominent supporter of American servicemembers.

00:05:11.120 --> 00:05:15.880
He's lended his talents as a narrator to various
military documentaries, entertained troops

00:05:15.880 --> 00:05:20.210
with the Lieutenant Dan Band, and created
his own philanthropic organization, the Gary

00:05:20.210 --> 00:05:24.240
Sinise Foundation, to support servicemembers
once they're back home on U.S. soil.

00:05:24.520 --> 00:05:28.770
Sinise has also been one of the few openly
Republican celebrities in Hollywood, founding

00:05:28.770 --> 00:05:33.840
a group for conservative actors known as the
"Friends of Abe" in 2004 and supporting John

00:05:33.840 --> 00:05:36.000
McCain's 2008 presidential campaign.

00:05:36.080 --> 00:05:40.920
However, he disassociated himself from the
organization prior to the 2016 election, and

00:05:40.930 --> 00:05:45.180
his online presence makes it clear that apart
from acting, his real priority is supporting

00:05:45.180 --> 00:05:45.760
the troops.

00:05:46.780 --> 00:05:51.080
The sleazy principal who admitted Forrest
to the public school system in exchange for

00:05:51.080 --> 00:05:56.180
a roll in the hay with Mrs. Gump will be forever
remembered for his awkward, well… this.

00:06:03.050 --> 00:06:06.820
But when it comes to this actor, you're more
likely to recognize him from the TV roles

00:06:06.820 --> 00:06:07.820
that followed.

00:06:07.820 --> 00:06:13.130
From 2005 through 2010, Anderson was a series
regular on Lost in the role of the kind-hearted

00:06:13.130 --> 00:06:16.771
crash survivor Bernard, and if you didn't
catch him in that, you might know him as the

00:06:16.780 --> 00:06:19.200
cold-hearted Lee Paxton on Justified.

00:06:19.480 --> 00:06:23.730
But as ubiquitous as he is onscreen, the actor
keeps a low profile off camera.

00:06:23.730 --> 00:06:28.130
He's been married to the same woman since
1985, is the father of twins, and in his spare

00:06:28.130 --> 00:06:29.910
time, he likes to write mysteries.

00:06:29.910 --> 00:06:33.820
In short, Anderson has gone on from Forrest
Gump to become what seems like the lifestyle

00:06:33.820 --> 00:06:37.730
of an average retired dad… except that he's
also one of the hardest-working character

00:06:37.730 --> 00:06:39.120
actors of his generation.

00:06:40.380 --> 00:06:45.220
If you've seen Forrest Gump, you'll recognize
Afemo Omilami as the frothing drill sergeant

00:06:45.220 --> 00:06:47.880
who complimented Forrest's intelligence, sort
of.

00:06:48.200 --> 00:06:50.700
"You must have a g--damn IQ of 160.

00:06:51.060 --> 00:06:53.220
You are g--damn gifted, Private Gump."

00:06:53.540 --> 00:06:58.080
The drill sergeant role was only a bit part
for Omilami, who was already a Hollywood veteran

00:06:58.080 --> 00:06:59.520
when Forrest Gump was made.

00:06:59.520 --> 00:07:03.880
Omilami has appeared in multiple projects
every year dating all the way back to 1990.

00:07:03.880 --> 00:07:08.630
Most recently, he held a major role in True
Detective and appeared as the Mayor of District

00:07:08.630 --> 00:07:10.770
11 in The Hunger Games: Catching Fire.

00:07:10.770 --> 00:07:15.670
And despite his busy work schedule, Omilami
also helps to run Hosea Feed the Hungry, an

00:07:15.670 --> 00:07:20.020
Atlanta-based charitable organization designed
to combat homelessness and food scarcity.

00:07:20.920 --> 00:07:25.100
It's practically the end of the movie before
he appears on screen, but he's there.

00:07:25.110 --> 00:07:29.340
Before he saw dead people, Haley Joel Osment
made his big-screen debut in the tiny role

00:07:29.340 --> 00:07:30.280
of Forrest Junior.

00:07:30.610 --> 00:07:34.260
Needless to say, it was a good jumping-off
point for Osment's career; he went on to become

00:07:34.260 --> 00:07:39.030
a Hollywood icon at the age of nine thanks
to his breakout performance in The Sixth Sense.

00:07:39.030 --> 00:07:42.920
He took a break to attend college, and while
his celebrity status has receded, he's not

00:07:42.920 --> 00:07:43.740
hurting for work.

00:07:43.960 --> 00:07:48.580
He recently reprised his role as Sora in the
third Kingdom Hearts game, and continues to

00:07:48.580 --> 00:07:52.020
appear in smaller parts in movies, TV, and
other weird projects.

00:07:53.140 --> 00:07:57.820
Character actor Geoffrey Blake portrayed the
loathsome Wesley, Jenny's abusive, bad-news

00:07:57.820 --> 00:07:58.320
boyfriend.

00:07:58.400 --> 00:08:02.420
He'd already appeared in dozens of movies
and TV shows before Forrest Gump, and he went

00:08:02.430 --> 00:08:04.620
right back to that hustle after filming his
part.

00:08:04.620 --> 00:08:09.370
You may have seen him in one of his many short
stints on shows like Renegade, NYPD Blue,

00:08:09.370 --> 00:08:12.160
multiple CSI series, Criminal Minds, and Grimm.

00:08:12.160 --> 00:08:15.980
And while they played enemies on screen, Blake
and Hanks must have gotten along just fine

00:08:15.980 --> 00:08:20.700
in real life; Blake went on to film small
parts for Hanks' Apollo 13 and Cast Away.

00:08:21.920 --> 00:08:26.800
When Siobhan Fallon Hogan appeared as the
hard-nut-to-crack bus driver in Forrest Gump,

00:08:26.800 --> 00:08:30.930
she'd just finished some small but memorable
work in two comedy institutions.

00:08:30.930 --> 00:08:34.899
She'd been a cast member on Saturday Night
Live for its seventeenth season in 1991 and

00:08:34.899 --> 00:08:39.120
'92, and had a recurring role on Seinfeld
as Tina, Elaine's weird roommate.

00:08:39.120 --> 00:08:43.149
Fallon Hogan has played many small parts since,
but she's also a frequent muse of provocative

00:08:43.149 --> 00:08:44.740
filmmaker Lars von Trier.

00:08:44.740 --> 00:08:49.480
But while she still works as an actor, she
left Hollywood behind long ago, choosing instead

00:08:49.480 --> 00:08:51.589
to live in suburban New Jersey with her family.

00:08:52.689 --> 00:08:56.720
When a nearly grown Forrest gets chased by
a bunch of bullies in a pickup truck, he's

00:08:56.720 --> 00:09:01.300
so fast he manages to outrun them, earning
the attention of legendary University of Alabama

00:09:01.300 --> 00:09:03.200
football coach Paul "Bear" Bryant.

00:09:03.380 --> 00:09:08.080
Forrest secures a sports scholarship and becomes
a reliable All-American playmaker who's eventually

00:09:08.089 --> 00:09:11.040
given the chance to meet President John F.
Kennedy.

00:09:11.040 --> 00:09:15.480
JFK may appear in the movie thanks to special
effects, but Bear Bryant is played by a flesh

00:09:15.480 --> 00:09:17.930
and blood actor named of Sonny Shroyer.

00:09:17.930 --> 00:09:20.100
It's nowhere near Shroyer's most famous work,
though.

00:09:20.240 --> 00:09:24.660
Prior to his Forrest Gump part, he played
Deputy Sheriff Enos on the popular TV series

00:09:24.660 --> 00:09:25.580
The Dukes of Hazzard.

00:09:25.800 --> 00:09:29.440
Shroyer was so likable in the role that he
got his own spinoff series, simply called

00:09:29.440 --> 00:09:30.680
Enos, in 1980.

00:09:30.900 --> 00:09:35.700
Shroyer was nearly 60 years old when Forrest
Gump was filmed, and his career has understandably

00:09:35.709 --> 00:09:37.540
slowed down a bit in the years since.

00:09:37.540 --> 00:09:42.160
He tended toward movies with ties to the American
South, including Ray, A Love Song for Bobby

00:09:42.160 --> 00:09:44.519
Long, and multiple adaptations of John Grisham
novels.

00:09:46.060 --> 00:09:49.670
When Forrest heads to New York City to check
on his old friend Lieutenant Dan, he finds

00:09:49.670 --> 00:09:52.259
that his former commanding officer isn't doing
well.

00:09:52.259 --> 00:09:56.060
He's found living in squalor, spending most
of his time drinking and cavorting with two

00:09:56.060 --> 00:10:00.580
women of questionable repute: "Long Limbs
Lenore" and "Cunning Carla."

00:10:00.580 --> 00:10:01.160
"Loser!

00:10:01.160 --> 00:10:01.860
Ya freak!"

00:10:02.200 --> 00:10:07.620
Marla Sucharetza, the actress who played Lenore,
is presumably a lot nicer than she comes across

00:10:07.620 --> 00:10:08.120
onscreen.

00:10:08.300 --> 00:10:12.559
Forrest Gump marked her first role in a major
movie, and in its wake, she's had a long career

00:10:12.560 --> 00:10:13.600
as a character actor.

00:10:13.960 --> 00:10:18.370
She's popped up in TV shows like Seinfeld,
Damages, and The Good Wife, and made multiple

00:10:18.370 --> 00:10:20.320
appearances on different Law &amp; Order series.

00:10:20.630 --> 00:10:25.420
She also appeared in movies such as The Station
Agent and the crude comedy Road Trip, in which

00:10:25.420 --> 00:10:28.399
she was credited as playing a "Sperm Bank
Nurse."

00:10:28.400 --> 00:10:30.220
Hey, acting isn't always glorious.

00:10:30.380 --> 00:10:33.920
Sometimes you're in a gross-out movie, and
sometimes you're in the cast of a beloved

00:10:33.920 --> 00:10:34.920
Best Picture.

00:10:35.320 --> 00:10:40.160
"Life is a box of chocolates, Forrest… ya
never know what you're gonna get."

